00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.100
Then we leave it as is.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.200
If nothing is chosen
in this section,

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.420
the defaults are taken.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:43.290
Now in this section, I get
to review my configurations.

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:46.180
And now click on Create.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:49.210
Now if you refresh it, you can
see that your load balancer

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:50.770
is here.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.810
Now that we've created
a load balancer,

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:54.520
let's quickly test it out.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.910
Click on this to get to
the load balancer details.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:02.260
Then go to Monitoring to
see the load balancing.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.490
We see this.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:05.710
Now let me go back
to the Details,

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:08.200
pick up the frontend
external IP address,

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.690
and go to a new tab or window.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:13.090
I've just opened up
an incognito window.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:16.240
Here, let me put
in the IP address.

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:19.000
And as you can see, you can
see the guestbook application

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.530
that we had deployed.

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:23.860
Now let me randomly
put in some load.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.703
Now, let's go back and
check our Monitoring queue.

00:13:26.703 --> 00:13:28.120
You see that there's
a load coming

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.310
in from different
continents across the globe

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:32.410
to the frontend and
hitting it and moving

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.570
to the assigned backend.

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:38.350
Now let me go back and add some
intense amount of load again.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:41.630
Let's quickly refresh
this, and here you go.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:44.560
You can see that there's so much
more load coming in from Asia

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.300
as opposed to America.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:49.030
And similarly, you can also
load balance it further

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:52.710
amongst different backends
internally and monitor them.

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:55.200
So we successfully
created and tested

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:57.630
our external load
balancer, bringing us

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:59.910
to the end of this demo.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:02.230
DEOK FILHO: Google Cloud's
